-- Blank titles refused everywhere (decided with the person 2026-10-14).
-- Generated by drizzle-kit, then HAND-EDITED (marked "HAND-EDITED" below),
-- the same way as 0032 and 0034.
--
-- The DTOs refuse a blank title since this step (common/validators/title.ts —
-- programs since 3b-2, templates now). These two CHECKs are the database's
-- half, like the workouts' *_name_not_blank: whatever writes a title — the
-- app, the seed, a query typed by hand — can't store one with nothing
-- visible in it. btrim() removes the spaces at both ends; a title of spaces
-- alone becomes '', of length 0.
--
-- Why hand-edited: ADD CONSTRAINT … CHECK checks EVERY existing row, and
-- fails the whole migration if one breaks it. Before this step the API
-- stored '' and '   ' as titles, so a database may hold some. They are
-- renamed first.

-- HAND-EDITED: the existing blank titles get a visible one — "Untitled
-- template" / "Untitled program" (the person's choice): it says plainly that
-- nobody named it, and the practitioner can rename it from the page. The
-- WHERE is the CHECK's own condition, negated, so exactly the rows the CHECK
-- would refuse change — no more: a title with spaces AROUND real words
-- ('  Knee  ') is valid and left as it is (decided too: only blanks).
--
-- These UPDATEs run as the tables' owner, which the closed-program guard
-- (0031) exempts — a closed or archived program with a blank title is
-- renamed too. They write no audit entry: an audit row needs the USER who
-- acted (audit_logs.performed_by is NOT NULL), and a migration has none.
-- This file, in version control, is the record of the change, as for the
-- backfills of 0032 and 0034.
UPDATE "program_templates"
SET "title" = 'Untitled template'
WHERE length(btrim("title")) = 0;--> statement-breakpoint
UPDATE "assigned_programs"
SET "title" = 'Untitled program'
WHERE length(btrim("title")) = 0;--> statement-breakpoint

-- Generated: the CHECKs themselves.
ALTER TABLE "assigned_programs" ADD CONSTRAINT "assigned_programs_title_not_blank" CHECK (length(btrim("assigned_programs"."title")) > 0);--> statement-breakpoint
ALTER TABLE "program_templates" ADD CONSTRAINT "program_templates_title_not_blank" CHECK (length(btrim("program_templates"."title")) > 0);